From a04d0733e58d47187508c87b252273f08482505f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): extend WO-B WIDE_DECODE to 128 rows and guard
 high-concurrency decode cliffs

Base: 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488 (spark-ds41f:1107 patch 0761).

Rationale:
1. At default max_num_seqs=16, CopyDrafter (K=5, V=16) widens max_decode_rows to 107 (16*6 + 11), capturing and replaying the 104-row and 112-row target FULL decode CUDA graphs (and up to 128 rows at max_num_seqs=21..32). At 97..128 rows, WO-A (_WO_A_TILES up to 128), fused_wqa_wkv ((3904, 5120) up to 128), shared_expert ((1024, 5120) up to 128), and vocab (ROW_TILES up to 128) all dispatch 128-row decode tiles, whereas WO-B ((5120, 3072) on TP3 ranks 0-1, (5120, 2048) on TP4 and TP3 rank 2, and (5120, 1024) on TP8) stopped at WIDE_DECODE {96: 96} and DECODE_FP8_CONFIGS {96}. Because TileLangWOProjection.tilelang_decode_rows is 128, WO-B fell back to DECODE_ROWS=64 (2x64 M-tiles x 40 N-tiles = 80 CTAs in 2 waves on 48 GB10 SMs, reading the 10-15 MiB weight matrix twice). Adding 128: dict(block_N=128, block_K=128, num_stages=2, threads=256) to DECODE_FP8_CONFIGS and 128: 128 to WIDE_DECODE launches 1x40 = 40 CTAs in a single wave on 48 SMs while staying on the unspecialized mxfp8_gemm_decode pipeline for padded decode workspaces, cutting WO-B latency by 13.8-16.9% on (5120, 3072), 13.3-18.0% on (5120, 2048), and 11.5-20.4% on (5120, 1024) across M=104..128.
2. When max_num_seqs > 32 (e.g. max_num_seqs=48, max_decode_rows=299), sp_prefill.resolve_min_rows previously took max(max_cudagraph_capture_size, max_decode_rows) + 1 = 300 even when max_cudagraph_capture_size <= 204, opening a 205..299-row gap above SparkNet One-Shot RoCE AllReduce (2 MiB = 204 rows at 5120 BF16) that ran uncaptured on PyNCCL. Bound sp_min_rows by max(max_cudagraph_capture_size + 1, roce_rows) when roce_rows > 0, warn when max_cudagraph_capture_size exceeds roce_rows, and route all_reduce_rank_order through roce_comm.reduce_scatter + roce_comm.all_gather whenever both halves are eligible (up to 408 rows on tp3-triangle / tp4-switched).
3. In dense_varlen_decode_shapes, bound full-depth per-request varlen decode captures (r, r*max_q) at _FULL_DEPTH_VARLEN_DECODE_MAX_REQS = 16 so max_num_seqs=32 and 48 reuse the 8-row/16-row padded FULL decode ladder for r > 16 instead of capturing 27-68 redundant full-depth target and DSpark context CUDA graphs (saving 138-142 MiB of graph pool memory at c32 and 346-422 MiB at c48).

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal across all M in 64..192 and K in 1024, 2048, 3072) for mxfp8_gemm and TileLangWOProjection; zero change to captured graphs at max_num_seqs <= 16.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_block_scale_words.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py tests/v1/cudagraph/test_cudagraph_manager.py (225 passed across 2 boots).

Upstream status: spark-ds41f DeepSeek-V4.1 SM121 TileLang / SparkNet / V1 CUDA graph runtime patch.

Split at selection for candidates 51-53: this patch keeps vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/gemm.py, vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/wo.py, tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py of the PR's patch; every kept line is unchanged.
